      "writtenOn": "2026-09-08T14:29:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "mDependencyMonitor is the last member, so only sizeof() changes; member offsets stay the same.\nAn A16+ blob would just allocate ~3120 extra bytes,I think which is harmless. The one real break would be a caller of getDependencyMonitor(), and any in-tree caller fails at compile time rather than silently.\nThat said, I don’t think this is the best approach myself. It changes the ABI for everyone just to accommodate one device’s prebuilts. I’ll look for a cleaner solution👀",
      "parentUuid": "abf42162_7b279922",
      "revId": "da95e1ddfd9d7cfa7ca4ead2d6a205da11388f65",
